                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Columbia SC",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 10 at 7:57PM EDT until October 10 at 10:00PM EDT by NWS Columbia SC",
                "description": "At 757 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 3 and 4 inches of rain have\nfallen. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the\nwarned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBatesburg-Leesville, Ridge Spring, Summit, Monetta, Ward, Hibernia,\nKneece, Fredonia, Delmar, Circle Fire Station, Murray, Cedar Grove\nFire Station, South Shore Marina, Riverbend Boat Ramp, Lake Murray\nShores, Hollow Creek Public Park, Oswald Park, Siesta Cove Marina\nand Shull Island.\n\nThis includes Interstate 20 in South Carolina between mile markers 24\nand 32.",
                "instruction": "Most flooding deaths occur in vehicles. Never drive through a flooded\nroadway or around barricades. Turn around, don't drown.",
                "response": "Avoid",
